  "summary": "CKEditor: Cross-site scripting (XSS) in the engine package",
  "details": "### Impact\nA Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability has been discovered in the CKEditor 5 engine. This vulnerability could be triggered by inserting specially crafted markup under a specific General HTML Support configuration that allows inserting objects, leading to unauthorized JavaScript code execution in a browser context isolated from the origin of the application embedding the editor.\n\nThis vulnerability affects only installations where General HTML Support is enabled and configured to allow the affected HTML content.\n\n### Patches\nThe problem has been recognized and patched. The fix will be available in version `48.5.1` (and above) and `47.7.4` (LTS).\n\n### For more information\nEmail us at [security@cksource.com](mailto:security@cksource.com) if you have any questions or comments about this advisory.",
